# Formats staged files before they are committed, so nothing reaches CI badly
# formatted and nobody has to fix formatting in a follow-up commit.
#
# Only staged files, so this stays fast. It rewrites what you are committing —
# after the repo-wide reformat that is a no-op in practice, and it stops a
# differently-configured editor from reintroducing drift.
#
# To commit without it, once: git commit --no-verify
npx lint-staged
